[recent-work.since-2026-11-01]
identity = "ADR-0001 (docs/adr/0001-identity-and-scope.md): identity resolved from code. The product is `jk`; measured coupling between the reversibility path and the key subsystem is zero in both directions, and the audit chain is library-only (main.rs never builds an AuditLog). Applied: `key-lifecycle` feature gates the jk-keys binary out of the default build; identity statements corrected in README, PROOF-NEEDS, ARCHITECTURE, januskey-cli/src/lib.rs, KEY_LIFECYCLE; V-1..V-3 ledger rows pin downstream consumption (valence-shell, ochrance, aletheia) as DESIGNED, since no repository outside this workspace depends on reversible-core. Not applied: the module move into crates/januskey-keys, which needs a toolchain this session does not have (no rustc, no crates.io) — steps and acceptance criteria in ADR-0001 §5."
human-action = "Two files contradict ADR-0001 and are agent-denied by the Trustfile (@trust-deny: modify-trustfile, modify-threat-model): contractiles/Trustfile.a2ml line 8 calls januskey \"a key-management tool\"; threat-model.a2ml [primitives.mac] still describes the removed home-rolled HMAC. Both need an owner edit."

claim-surfaces = "Estate consistency audit (docs/estate/2026-11-01-handoff-and-consistency-audit.md) found the structural model intact and the drift in this repo's own published surfaces. Corrected for over-claim only: wiki theory pages (rmo, rmr, mpr, maa-framework, formal-model, index) restated at the strength of the claims ledger; security/THREAT_MODEL.adoc compliance mapping rewritten and its '256-bit ECC' and BLAKE3 rows removed (neither is in the tree); CLI about/long_about and the Obliterate help no longer claim provable reversibility or a GDPR determination; crate descriptions and module headers aligned; TOPOLOGY diagram label de-claimed. No ledger row changed status and no test or proof count changed."

